  "publicDayTitleAccent": "Amaya’s circle",
  "publicDayLede": "School systems are good at records and bad at relationships. Parents hear nothing until something goes wrong, and teachers get messages at 10 pm. Circle uses what a school already records to keep families close. Here is a Monday for Amaya, Year 4 Emerald.",
  "publicDayArriveTime": "07:42",
  "publicDayArriveTag": "The day, as it happens",
  "publicDayArriveTitle": "Amaya’s mum sees she’s arrived",
  "publicDayArriveBody": "The gate scan and the register start a ring of Amaya’s day on her mum’s phone. Lessons, lunch and the bus home appear as they happen. Nobody had to send a message.",
  "publicDayMomentTime": "08:55",
  "publicDayMomentTag": "Moments",
  "publicDayMomentTitle": "Her teacher shares a moment in ten seconds",
  "publicDayMomentBody": "Ms. Jayasinghe taps Amaya’s name, picks Photo, writes a line and tags the skill she noticed. Only Amaya’s family sees it, and only if the family has agreed to photos.",
  "publicDayGrandmaTime": "09:10",
  "publicDayGrandmaTag": "Family circle",
  "publicDayGrandmaTitle": "Grandma in Kandy loves it too",
  "publicDayGrandmaBody": "Parents can invite up to four relatives to see moments. Grandparents never see fees, results, attendance or health, and can be removed with one tap.",
  "publicDayPeopleTime": "12:30",
  "publicDayPeopleTag": "Everyone around the child",
  "publicDayPeopleTitle": "Dad sees who looks after Amaya",
  "publicDayPeopleBody": "Every teacher, the coach and the nurse, with what each is working on with Amaya and when they reply. Saying thank you is one tap, and it reaches the teacher.",
  "publicDayTryTime": "18:20",
  "publicDayTryTag": "This week in class",
  "publicDayTryTitle": "They try one thing at home",
  "publicDayTryBody": "Each week teachers share what the class is learning and one small thing to try at home. Amaya and her mum write a postcard to Grandma, tap We tried it, and Ms. Jayasinghe sees it the next morning.",
  "publicDayQuietTime": "19:30",
  "publicDayQuietTag": "Quiet hours",
  "publicDayQuietTitle": "Teachers get their evenings back",
  "publicDayQuietBody": "A parent can still write at 19:30. Quad tells them kindly that it reaches the teacher at 07:00, and holds the teacher’s notifications until morning. Urgent safety alerts always go through.",
  "publicDayRecapTime": "Fri",
  "publicDayRecapTag": "Weekly recap",
  "publicDayRecapTitle": "A week with Amaya, in one card",
  "publicDayRecapBody": "The moments, the skills her teachers noticed, days in school, what the family tried at home, and one idea for the weekend.",
  "publicDayFoot": "Families choose who sees photos of their child. Nothing about health or safeguarding ever goes into Circle.",
  "publicDayQuietClock": "07:00",
